# Fizzlestiks-attack.lic
# Bigshot custom attack routine for Fizzlestiks (Bard). Drop it into a bigshot
# hunting-commands list as a single command, replacing "feint (s9), attack (xx)":
#
#   script Fizzlestiks-attack
#
# bigshot pauses itself, runs this once against the target it already has
# locked, then resumes to loot / wander / retarget -- so this does exactly ONE
# attack decision per call and returns; bigshot re-invokes it every pass while
# the target is still up. Same shape as Brayis-attack.lic, minus the tackle.
#
# Rhythm (what "feint (s9), attack (xx)" did): bigshot expands that list to one
# feint plus five attacks ((xx) is five) and runs it top to bottom per target,
# so it's a feint, five swings, a feint, and so on. This keeps that rhythm
# across calls in $fizzlestiks_attack_rhythm ([target id, swings since the
# feint]): a new target opens with a feint, then five plain attacks, then the
# next feint.
#
#   The feint goes only if Lich's own CMan.available? says so -- it folds in
#   "known", enough stamina, off cooldown, and not overexerted, so there's no
#   hardcoded stamina number here to drift out of date. If it isn't available,
#   that slot is a plain attack instead, the way (s9) skipped the feint.
#
# 10/30 12:34: the first version feinted on EVERY pass while stamina lasted --
# ten feints on one hobgoblin, about 30 s, before the first swing.
#
# Deliberately does NOT switch back to stance defensive -- bigshot's own
# hunting/wander stance settings take over once this returns.
#
# Disarm: nothing in the RIGHT hand means the weapon is gone (the left holds
# the hunting tambourine, so "both hands empty" would never be true). Don't
# fall back to punching -- Brayis died doing that. Fizzlestiks-disarmguard.lic
# is what actually goes after the weapon; this just refuses to fight bare-
# fisted in the meantime, and if the guard isn't running, sends bigshot to rest
# the same way Salvi/Picko's attack routines do.

# --- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Monster-agnostic death check: bigshot itself never text-matches kill messages
# (they vary per creature) -- it reads GameObj status, which Lich core keeps
# current from the room/combat XML. A dead creature reads "dead" while the
# corpse lingers, then "gone" once it decays or is looted.
def target_dead?(foe)
  return true if foe.nil?
  return true if foe.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/
  !GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

# Plain attack with whatever weapon is in hand. No-ops if the target is already
# dead.
def plain_attack(foe)
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  fput "attack"
  waitrt?
end

# Feint if Lich says it's usable right now. CMan.use waits out roundtime first
# and returns the answering line, or nil if it never sent anything.
# @return [Boolean] true if a feint was actually sent
def try_feint(foe)
  return false unless CMan.available?("feint", target: foe)
  !CMan.use("feint", foe).nil?
end

# --- main ----------------------------------------------------------------

foe = GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.id.to_i == XMLData.current_target_id.to_i } if XMLData.current_target_id
foe ||= GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }

# nothing (live) to hit -- hand control straight back to bigshot, which loots
exit if target_dead?(foe)

fput "target ##{foe.id}" unless XMLData.current_target_id.to_i == foe.id.to_i

waitrt?

exit if target_dead?(foe)

if checkright.nil?
  echo "########## NO WEAPON IN RIGHT HAND -- not fighting bare-fisted ##########"
  unless Script.running?("Fizzlestiks-disarmguard")
    echo "## Fizzlestiks-disarmguard isn't running -- asking bigshot to rest"
    $bigshot_should_rest = true
    $rest_reason = "Disarmed"
  end
  exit
end

fput "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"

last_id, swings = $fizzlestiks_attack_rhythm
swings = nil unless last_id == foe.id # new target: open with a feint
if (swings.nil? || swings >= 5) && try_feint(foe)
  $fizzlestiks_attack_rhythm = [foe.id, 0]
else
  plain_attack(foe)
  $fizzlestiks_attack_rhythm = [foe.id, swings.to_i + 1]
end
